 "title": "Stack Frames",
 "desc": "Goal: Understand the function prologue and epilogue — the setup and teardown of every function's stack frame. Prologue: push ebp; mov ebp,esp; sub esp,N. Epilogue: leave (= mov esp,ebp; pop ebp). Local variables live at negative offsets from EBP.",
 "arch": "x86",
 "word": 4,
 "hexW": 8,
